    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.sessions\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen Saving and Restoring a Session with Neo-Tree open, an Empty Buffer gets restored. This buffer also isn't recognized as Neotree as running :Neotree toggle, open another Neo-tree Instance.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Install mini.sessions and neo-tree\r\n- require('mini.sessions').write('testing')\r\n- restart neovim\r\n- require('mini.sessions').read('testing')\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe best option would be to properly restore Neo-tree to how it was. If this isn't possible, allowing the exclusion of certain buffer types from the Session might works as a workaround. I personally don't need Neo-Tree to be restored with the Session. This can be done with the existing hooks in the settings. But this means that Neo-Tree will always be closed when loading or saving a Session.\r\nWether properly saving and loading neo-tree status is in scope of this project, is another question.",
    "closed_at": "2024-01-25T10:01:23Z",
