            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I ran into this as well and used the `hook` workaround at first. Then I found out that I could also adjust the session options not to save ~blank buffers~ empty windows (as per `:h sessionoptions`):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- don't save blank buffers to sessions (like neo-tree, trouble etc.)\r\nvim.opt.sessionoptions:remove('blank')\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt doesn't restore Neo-Tree on session read, but it does prevent blank windows.",
